# Post–major change: docs and Cursor sync

When a change is **cross-cutting** (new product modes, routing shells, auth/workspace model, OpenAPI contract, import/layer conventions, or repo structure), treat **documentation + Cursor artifacts** as part of the same deliverable as the code.

## When this applies

- New or renamed **route shells**, dashboards, or navigation contracts (web/mobile).
- **Workspace / identity** UX shifts (`useActiveWorkspace`, allowed workspaces, session persistence).
- **OpenAPI** schema or codegen changes that affect client/server types.
- New **always-on constraints** or ESLint/package-structure rules (rare — see `.cursor/README.md` always-on cap).
- New **repeatable workflows** that engineers or agents should follow (prefer a **skill** under `.cursor/skills/`).

## Checklist (do not skip)

Use the full checklist: [documentation/internal/post-major-change-checklist.md](../../../documentation/internal/post-major-change-checklist.md).

Minimum bar before calling the work “done”:

1. **`documentation/`** — Add or update the relevant guide under `documentation/client/` or `documentation/server/`; add a row to that folder’s `README.md` when it is a new long-form doc.
2. **`.cursor/rules/`** — If behavior is now constrained or patterned differently, update the smallest set of `.mdc` files (or add one **scoped** rule with `globs`; do not increase always-on rule count without replacing an existing always-on rule — see `.cursor/README.md`).
3. **`AGENTS.md` / `.cursor/README.md`** — Update only when onboarding or extension process changes.
4. **`documentation/internal/cursor-audit-latest.md`** — Refresh the inventory table when rules, skills, or agents are added/removed/renamed.

## Examples

```markdown
// ✅ DO — Same PR or fast-follow: workspace shells land + `documentation/client/architecture/workspace-first-architecture.md` updated
// ❌ DON'T — Large routing refactor with no doc or rule touch; the next agent will re-derive intent from diff noise only
```

Long prose and file maps belong in **`documentation/`**, not in bloated `.mdc` bodies (see `documentation.mdc`).
